From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: mediatek: include RPS and RX queue definitions

Compile-only candidate for Nothing B4.1 ee2be53cb75670b548948636a0db1d1ff112bf12.
Linux 6.18 no longer provides these structures through netdevice.h.
This does not validate RPS map update serialization or enable modem runtime.

Signed-off-by: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/rps/rps_perf.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/rps/rps_perf.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/rps/rps_perf.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/rps/rps_perf.c
@@ -27,6 +27,8 @@
 #include <linux/tcp.h>
 #include <linux/ipv6.h>
 #include <net/ipv6.h>
+#include <net/netdev_rx_queue.h>
+#include <net/rps.h>
 #include <net/sch_generic.h>
 #include <linux/skbuff.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
